3b. Per-edge fields (one dict per entry in prg_edges)
Field
Type
Notes
neighbor_name
str
which detected object this edge is against
relation_prediction
str | None
"Contact" / "Support" / "Separate", from classify_relation(). "Contact" and "Separate" are direct model outputs (logistic_model.joblib, trained on physics-verified gazebo_contact, binary). "Support" is NOT a model output — it's a post-hoc split of the model's "Contact" class using a relative_height threshold (SUPPORT_RELATIVE_HEIGHT_THRESHOLD, currently a placeholder value pending Step 6 tuning against training_data_v3_metric_only.csv's heuristic_label). The model was never trained on a 3-way target — treat this distinction as load-bearing for any downstream per-class analysis.
relation_confidence
float | None
classify_relation()'s confidence. Only meaningful as stated for "Contact"/"Separate" predictions — it is the binary model's predict_proba for touching-vs-not. For "Support" predictions, this is the same binary confidence carried over from before the post-hoc split — it is NOT a calibrated confidence in the Support/Contact distinction itself, since the model was never asked to estimate one. Do not aggregate this field across relation_prediction groups without accounting for this.
prg_edge_error
float
from compute_prg_edge_error(), range [0,1]. Always a scalar, never None — code-confirmed: geometric ambiguity falls back to 0.5 (neutral), not None. Polarity: 0 = boundary reliably consistent, 1 = likely unreliable — same direction as Gap (higher = worse), confirmed against confidence_term/geometric_term logic; get explicit one-line confirmation from collaborator before relying on this for the two-signal conformal gate.
geometric_feature_vector
dict | None
the dict from LiveDepthFeatureSource.compute(), logged in full for reproducibility. Contains 9 keys, not 8: the 8 model features plus minimum_boundary_distance_is_metric (a bool metadata flag, dropped before the vector is fed to the classifier — not itself a 9th feature). Don't reshape this into an 8-element array without dropping that key first.
mask_is_bbox_placeholder
bool
True if mask_a/mask_b for this edge were bbox-rectangle placeholders rather than real segmentation masks. Collaborator-confirmed: boundary_sharpness, edge_continuity, and occlusion_boundary_score are systematically distorted (not just noisier) on rectangle masks. Any edge with this flag True is wiring-validation only, never a reportable number.

