4. The real interface contract
def get_prg_edge_error(
    rgb, depth, target_name: str, all_object_masks: dict[str, "np.ndarray"],
    trial_id: str, camera_intrinsics: "CameraIntrinsics",
) -> list[dict]:
    """
    integration/prg_client.py — thin sequencing wrapper only, no logic of
    its own (collaborator's explicit design note: if decision logic
    accumulates here, it belongs in one of the three stages below).

    Calls, in order, for every pair returned by enumerate_adjacent_pairs()
    that contains target_name:
        1. LiveDepthFeatureSource(camera_intrinsics).compute(depth, mask_a, mask_b)
           -> features: dict (9 keys — see 3b note)
        2. classify_relation(features) -> (relation: str, confidence: float)
           NaN in any of the 8 model features raises ValueError here —
           this is an EXPECTED failure mode (missing open3d, non-overlapping
           masks), not necessarily a bug. See Section 6.
        3. compute_prg_edge_error(rgb, depth, target_bbox, relation, confidence,
                                    mask_a, mask_b) -> float  (always scalar, never None)

    Returns a list of per-edge dicts (Section 3b shape), or [] if
    target_name has no adjacent objects this frame. Falls back to a
    single seeded-stub entry (Section 3a, prg_is_stub=True) if
    config["use_stub"] is set, camera_intrinsics is missing, or the real
    chain raises for any reason -- a crash in the collaborator's code
    must never kill this pipeline's own Gap logging or the trial.
    """

