5. Mask provenance
No segmentation model currently exists in either pipeline for real hardware (the sim path used Gazebo's semantic camera, which has no real-hardware equivalent). Until one exists:
all_object_masks values are bbox-rectangle placeholders (bbox_to_mask() in prg_client.py).
Every edge computed from placeholder masks is flagged mask_is_bbox_placeholder=True (Section 3b).
Fastest real path, per collaborator: SAM prompted with the existing detector's bboxes — no training required. Not built today; smoke-testing proceeds on placeholders in the meantime.
Any prg_edges entry with mask_is_bbox_placeholder=True is excluded from reportable analysis — wiring/smoke-test validation only, per collaborator's explicit warning that boundary-dependent features are systematically (not just noisily) distorted on rectangles.

6. Stub status and expected failure modes
A stub get_prg_edge_error() path returning a single seeded-random entry (prg_is_stub=True) is wired into the pipeline exactly where the real chain will eventually go, verified end-to-end via test_prg_stub_integration.py: stub → TrialRecord → TrialLogger.append_trial() → JSONL on disk → load_trials() — confirmed the same value round-trips intact.
daily_integration_check.py runs end-to-end from the moment the collaborator's code lands, without waiting on her real implementation.
logger.py's schema round-trip is confirmed for prg_edges/prg_is_stub before any real data exists.
NEW — known, expected causes of prg_is_stub=True on a real-chain attempt (i.e. not config["use_stub"]), so these aren't re-diagnosed from scratch mid-collection:
surface_normal_consistency returns NaN when open3d isn't installed in the running environment, or when mask_a/mask_b don't sufficiently overlap in the point cloud — classify_relation() raises ValueError on any NaN feature, triggering the stub fallback.
Missing or malformed camera_intrinsics.
Any other exception in the three-stage chain — always check prg_error_note first; it carries the actual exception string rather than requiring a re-run to reproduce.
Explicitly: nothing computed against this stub, or against mask_is_bbox_placeholder=True edges, is ever a real finding. Both are placeholders, not data.

